<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        The <a href="/manage/music-schedule">Music Schedule</a> chooses what plays, and how loud, at each time
        of day. The kiosks at the location then switch on their own, for example a quieter playlist before
        opening and music off after closing.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="Setting it up">
        <ol>
            <li>Choose the <strong>Location</strong>.</li>
            <li>Select <strong>Add part of the day</strong>. Give it a <strong>Name</strong>, tick the <strong>Days</strong>, and set when
                it <strong>Starts (UK time)</strong> and <strong>Ends</strong>. A part can run past midnight.</li>
            <li>Choose a <strong>Playlist</strong>, or <strong>Music off (pause)</strong>.</li>
            <li>Optionally tick <strong>Set the volume</strong>. Otherwise each kiosk keeps the volume it's at.</li>
            <li>When the week looks right, turn on <strong>Use this schedule</strong>.</li>
        </ol>
        <FluentText>
            Kiosks switch at the end of the song that's playing. Times with nothing scheduled leave the music
            as it is. If someone changes the music by hand, that
            lasts until the next part of the day starts.
        </FluentText>
        <HelpNote>
            The schedule only controls kiosks whose location is set. An Admin sets it on
            <a href="/manage/clients">Clients</a>, in the kiosk's <strong>Settings</strong> on the <strong>General</strong> tab.
        </HelpNote>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
